I gave her an English name before I ever saw her face.\
This was 2021. I was thirty-two and had been in Canada for eleven years. I had a house in Toronto whose mortgage took half my paycheck, a job at a financial data company in midtown, and a habit, that summer, of writing posts on a Chinese question-and-answer site called Zhihu late at night when I could not sleep. Most are political or social comentary like all guys do. Angry, lonely, and had just a little big of success to show and a little bit of self-claimed wisdom to share what I think was the world.\
One of the posts was a personal ad. I was feeling pressure from my parents who I live in the same household. You need to get a girlfriend soon, you need to start a family. Some may call this classic Asian parents, but all my white friends who has a half-decent job are way ahead of me in this area.\
The ad says:\
31, single, in Toronto, masters degree in Math from Uoft, Software Engineer. 175cm, 80kg, I total 500kg in big 3 lifts, I love working out, I ran half marathon. Own my house and car. Looking for a girlfriend, no less than 160cm, and must be pretty.\
And in the ad: I am vein like this.\
I didn't say those 2 things didn't happen in the same time. The half marathon was 3 years ago, the 500kg lifts was done this year. I said I am 31 since it is technically true, as many people born in my time in China, the government mistakenly put my birthday from Jan 03 to Nov 03.\
It quickly got some attention. Some one left a message: why someone like him doesn't have a girlfriend already, must be either fishing(
\f2 \'b5\'f6\'d3\'e3\'a3\'a9
\f1 or super ugly.\
I was read the comments/messaages over and over again until one caught my eye.\
"Can we be friends first? I really liked your post on Nietche's eternal return? Here is my wechat number *****"\
\
